@event ilse_village
# en: The Girl at the Bakery
title [a7ff00] = 面包店里的女孩
# en: In the village bakery a girl in white furs is trying to pay for a bun with a coin so cold it has frozen to the counter. The baker is losing patience. You recognise those eyes: they're Kael's. "Ilse," she says, before you ask. "Don't."
text [7c5df9] = 村里的面包店里，一个穿白色毛皮的女孩正想用一枚硬币买个小面包——那硬币冷得已经冻在了柜台上。面包师快没耐心了。你认得那双眼睛：是凯尔的。“伊尔泽，”不等你开口她就说，“别问。”
# en: A village bakery counter, a pale girl in white furs pushing a coin that is visibly frosted across the wood, a baffled baker.
scene [1cd5c0] = 村里面包店的柜台前，一个穿白色毛皮的苍白女孩把一枚明显结了霜的硬币推过木台，面包师一脸困惑。
# en: Pay for her bun
opt.left.label [31d334] = 替她付面包钱
# en: She stares at the bun, then at you, as if kindness is a trick she hasn't learned the counter to yet. "Fine," she says. "Thank you. Fine."
opt.left.say.1 [7b1308] = 她盯着面包，又盯着你，好像善意是一种她还没学会破解的把戏。“好吧，”她说，“谢谢。好吧。”
# en: Leave her to it
opt.right.label [d94459] = 随她去
# en: You leave. Through the window you see the coin crack, and the baker's breath freeze in the air. Ilse walks out with the bun. Nobody stops her.
opt.right.say.1 [1e970f] = 你走了。透过窗户，你看见那枚硬币裂开，面包师呼出的气在空中结成了冰。伊尔泽拿着面包走了出来。没人拦她。

@event ilse_frost_lessons
# en: A Trade in Winter
title [9ac35e] = 冬日的交易
# en: Ilse finds you by the frozen pond. "My brother won't talk to me. You will. Tell me how he really is, and I'll teach you Northern frost-craft. It's better than anything your professors know."
text [5847bc] = 伊尔泽在结冰的池塘边找到你。“我哥哥不跟我说话。你会。告诉我他现在到底过得怎么样，我就教你北境霜术。比你那些教授懂的都强。”
# en: A frozen pond at the edge of the woods, a girl in white furs drawing a perfect hexagon of frost in the air, a student copying her clumsily.
scene [4361bc] = 树林边结冰的池塘，一个穿白色毛皮的女孩在空中画出一个完美的六角霜花，一名学生笨拙地跟着模仿。
# en: Tell her the truth about Kael
opt.left.label [63ce17] = 把凯尔的实情告诉她
# en: You tell her about the cold hands, the roof at three in the morning, the bread. She listens without moving. Then she teaches you to freeze a falling leaf mid-air.
opt.left.say.1 [1bc603] = 你告诉她那双冰冷的手、凌晨三点的屋顶、那些面包。她一动不动地听着。然后她教你让一片飘落的叶子在半空中冻住。
# en: Protect Kael's privacy
opt.right.label [4b5f67] = 守住凯尔的隐私
# en: "He can tell you himself," you say. Ilse's eyes go flat. But the next day, she's at the pond again. "Fine. I'll teach you anyway. You'll need it."
opt.right.say.1 [91c9be] = “他可以自己告诉你，”你说。伊尔泽的眼神冷了下来。但第二天，她又出现在池塘边。“行吧。我还是教你。你会用得上的。”

@event ilse_grey_returns
# en: The Man in Grey Comes for Ilse
title [4eacc9] = 灰衣人来带走伊尔泽
# en: Late at night, a lane behind the bakery. The man in grey has one hand on Ilse's shoulder. "Home," he is saying softly. "Your family is waiting. The door is waiting." Ilse sees you. She doesn't call out. She just looks.
text [4c620a] = 深夜，面包店后面的小巷。灰衣人一只手搭在伊尔泽肩上。“回家吧，”他轻声说，“你的家人在等你。那扇门在等你。”伊尔泽看见了你。她没有呼救，只是看着你。
# en: A moonlit village lane, a man in a grey coat with one hand on a girl's shoulder, frost and shadow coiling around them both.
scene [fb6082] = 月光下的村中小巷，一个穿灰色外套的男人一只手搭在女孩肩上，霜与阴影缠绕在两人周围。
# en: Step between them
opt.left.label [f242e3] = 挡在他们之间
# en: Your spell breaks his grip. He looks at his frosted hand with mild surprise, bows, and walks into the dark. Ilse is shaking. "Nobody's ever — " she says, and stops.
opt.left.say.1 [f2b4a9] = 你的咒语打断了他的手。他略带惊讶地看着自己结霜的手，鞠了一躬，走进了黑暗。伊尔泽在发抖。“从来没有人——”她说，然后停住了。
# en: He swats your spell aside like a moth. When you get up, the lane is empty except for a single white glove in the snow.
opt.left.say.2 [eaa8cd] = 他像拍飞蛾一样拍开了你的咒语。等你爬起来，巷子里已空无一人，只有雪地上的一只白手套。
# en: Run for Kael
opt.right.label [839eee] = 跑去找凯尔
# en: Kael arrives like a blizzard. The man in grey takes one look at him and leaves without a word. Brother and sister stand in the snow, not touching, not speaking.
opt.right.say.1 [69e63e] = 凯尔像一场暴风雪般赶到。灰衣人只看了他一眼，便一言不发地离开了。兄妹俩站在雪里，没有碰触，没有说话。
# en: By the time you're back with help, the lane is empty. There's frost on the cobbles in the shape of a closed door.
opt.right.say.2 [8c5d56] = 等你带着帮手回来，巷子已经空了。鹅卵石上的霜结成了一扇紧闭的门的形状。

@event ilse_kael_reunion
# en: Brother and Sister
title [2c92a4] = 兄与妹
# en: Kael and Ilse have been in the same village for weeks and have spoken eleven words to each other. You have three cups of tea, a frozen jetty and a very bad idea.
text [210c93] = 凯尔和伊尔泽在同一个村子里待了好几个星期，一共只对彼此说了十一个字。你有三杯茶、一座结冰的栈桥，和一个非常糟糕的主意。
# en: Two pale siblings on opposite ends of a frozen jetty, a third person between them holding three cups of tea.
scene [d059c4] = 结冰栈桥的两端各坐着一个苍白的兄妹，中间一个人端着三杯茶。
# en: Sit them both down
opt.left.label [05e582] = 让他俩坐下来谈
# en: It takes an hour and two cups of tea are frozen solid. Then Ilse says "I was scared," and Kael says "So was I," and you quietly leave them to it.
opt.left.say.1 [75d491] = 花了一个钟头，有两杯茶冻成了冰坨。然后伊尔泽说：“我很害怕。”凯尔说：“我也是。”你悄悄离开，把时间留给他们。
# en: They argue in a language you don't speak, at a temperature you can't endure. But they argue — which, you suspect, is a start.
opt.left.say.2 [299f28] = 他们用一种你听不懂的语言、在一种你受不了的温度里吵架。但他们在吵——你猜，这算是个开始。
# en: Let them find their own way
opt.right.label [a54eb8] = 让他们自己找到路
# en: You leave the tea on the jetty. A week later you see them walking by the lake together, a careful arm's length apart. Then less.
opt.right.say.1 [79a710] = 你把茶留在栈桥上。一星期后，你看见他们一起沿着湖边散步，小心地隔着一臂远。后来就没那么远了。

@event ilse_northern_letter
# en: A Summons From the North
title [2572c4] = 来自北方的召唤
# en: A letter with a black-star seal. The Dumont family summons Ilse home. "If I don't go, they'll send someone worse than the man in grey," she says. "If I do go, I could tell them to their faces that it's over. Or they could keep me."
text [97b031] = 一封盖着黑星封印的信。杜蒙家族召伊尔泽回家。“如果我不去，他们会派一个比灰衣人更糟的人来，”她说，“如果我去了，我可以当面告诉他们一切都结束了。或者，他们会把我留下。”
# en: A girl holding a letter sealed with a black star, standing at a window that looks north toward far white mountains.
scene [4e2efd] = 一个女孩手握盖着黑星封印的信，站在一扇朝北的窗前，远处是白茫茫的群山。
# en: "Go. Tell them it's over."
opt.left.label [6759bb] = “去吧，告诉他们结束了。”
# en: She leaves on the dawn barge, chin up. Before she goes, she presses her forehead to yours, a Northern farewell. "If I'm not back by graduation," she says, "come and get me."
opt.left.say.1 [fae690] = 她坐黎明的驳船走了，下巴抬得高高的。走之前，她把额头贴在你额头上——北境的告别礼。“如果毕业前我没回来，”她说，“就来接我。”
# en: "Stay. Let them come."
opt.right.label [ef10a1] = “留下，让他们来。”
# en: She stays. She sews a sliver of winter into your collar "in case they do come". Nobody does. Not yet.
opt.right.say.1 [3114b6] = 她留了下来。她把一缕冬天缝进你的衣领，“万一他们真的来了”。没有人来。至少现在还没有。

@event ilse_farewell
# en: Snow in Blossomtide
title [224b90] = 花潮月的雪
# en: It's spring, the orchard is in full blossom, and it is snowing — gently, over one tree. Ilse is underneath it. "Graduation's soon," she says. "Everyone's leaving. I wanted to give you something before you forgot me."
text [ccd97c] = 春天，果园里繁花盛开，却下起了雪——轻轻地，只落在一棵树上。伊尔泽就站在树下。“快毕业了，”她说，“大家都要走了。我想在你忘记我之前送你点东西。”
# en: A single snowflake falling in a spring orchard full of blossom, a girl in white furs catching it on her glove and holding it out.
scene [63dad1] = 繁花盛开的春日果园里飘落一片雪花，一个穿白色毛皮的女孩用手套接住它，递了过来。
# en: "I won't forget you."
opt.left.label [6d1b23] = “我不会忘记你的。”
# en: She doesn't believe you, but she smiles anyway — the first real smile you've seen on her. She gives you a snowflake that never melts.
opt.left.say.1 [48bf7c] = 她不相信你，但还是笑了——你第一次在她脸上看到真正的笑容。她送给你一片永不融化的雪花。
# en: Invite her to the graduation
opt.right.label [d72a91] = 邀请她来参加毕业典礼
# en: "Me? At a graduation?" She looks horrified, and then, slowly, delighted. On the day, she sits next to Kael in the second row and cries more than anyone.
opt.right.say.1 [55ef3a] = “我？去毕业典礼？”她一脸惊恐，然后，慢慢地，变成了欣喜。那天，她坐在第二排凯尔身边，哭得比谁都厉害。
